  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level from all outcomes (2500, 2400, 0), computing deviations, and preferring the lottery with the higher probability of positive deviations (which is B, with 34%). The individual, however, focuses only on the probability of winning (non-zero outcome), misperceives it (believes A has higher chance), and uses this as justification. There is no mention of an aspiration level, averaging outcomes, or evaluating outcomes relative to a reference point. The information considered (winning probability) and the justification (higher chance of winning) do not align with the aspiration-level-based reason. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used this specific decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
